  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nBuild a planar concrete frame with bays 5 m and 7 m and story heights 3.3 m, 4.0 m and 3.1 m. The floor elevations are 3.3 m, 7.3 m and 10.4 m. Fix all three column bases. Both beams on floors 1, 2 and 3 carry downward full-span loads of 12, 10 and 8 kN/m, respectively, in case D. The completed property appendix specifies C30 concrete (E=30000 MPa, nu=0.2, G=12500 MPa, density=2500 kg/m^3), 500x500 mm columns C1 and 300x600 mm beams B1. Run a first-order linear elastic Euler-Bernoulli analysis in OpenSees with self weight off. Report ux, uz and ry at every column line on every floor; signed horizontal story displacement differences ux(upper)-ux(lower) at all nine column segments; Fx, Fz and My at all three bases; and local M2 at both ends of every first-story column. Use the exact cumulative elevations.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
        "output-requests.json",
        "analysis-conventions.txt"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
